  "protocol": "E2 requires SmartHealth v3 family-specific canonical raw products, feature products, and condition-stratified 2-development/1-test logical-cell splits. Their source-time event identity, inferred CC/CV boundary, 3.45–3.58 V CC selection, nominal-C-rate 0.25C–0.05C CV selection, and calibration-derived label_capacity_Ah are fixed in adjacent provenance files. The unified target is label_capacity_Ah / fixed domain nominal capacity (40 Ah for LISHEN; 280 Ah for CATL/EVE), consistent with XJTU/MIT. A condition without exactly three eligible logical sequences remains an explicit manual-confirmation stop, never a fallback split. This all-public Unified configuration is still planned until its formal multi-domain training/selection protocol is intentionally executed."
